// Title: Run Once Task Configuration in Registry
// ID: c74d7efc-8826-45d9-b8bb-f04fac9e4eff
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Avneet Singh @v3t0_, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-11-15
// Tags: attack.persistence, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1112
// Description: Rule to detect the configuration of Run Once registry key. Configured payload can be run by runonce.exe /AlternateShellStartup
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\Microsoft\\Active Setup\\Installed Components") AND where(TargetObject IENDSWITH "\\StubPath")) AND NOT ((((where(Details ICONTAINS "C:\\Program Files\\Google\\Chrome\\Application\\") AND where(Details ICONTAINS "\\Installer\\chrmstp.exe\" --configure-user-settings --verbose-logging --system-level"))) OR ((where(Details ICONTAINS "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\") OR where(Details ICONTAINS "C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\")) AND where(Details IENDSWITH "\\Installer\\setup.exe\" --configure-user-settings --verbose-logging --system-level --msedge --channel=stable")))))
